.TH XUR.STD.RE.DOTNET.IL2CPP 7 "2026-10-29" "xur 0.1.2" "Xur Manual"
.SH NAME
xur.std.re.dotnet.il2cpp \- read Unity Il2Cpp games
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B std::re::dotnet::il2cpp
reads the metadata and type table of a Unity Il2Cpp game.
.B Game
is the entry point: it opens a game folder, finds the
.B global\-metadata.dat
and
.B GameAssembly
binary, and gives every type, field and method by name.
It can also generate .NET proxy assemblies with
.BR write_assemblies() .
.PP
Backed by
.BR hao\-il2cpp .
.SH FUNCTIONS
.TP
.B open(path)
Open a game folder (the one holding
.B GameAssembly.so
and
.BR *_Data ).
Returns
.BR Result<Game,\ str> .
.TP
.B from_files(metadata, binary)
Open from explicit paths to
.B global\-metadata.dat
and
.BR GameAssembly .
Returns
.BR Result<Game,\ str> .
.SH Game METHODS
.TP
.B types()
A list of every
.B TypeView
in the game.
.TP
.B find_type(full_name)
Look up a type by its full name (e.g.\&
.BR \(dqSystem.String\(dq ).
Returns
.BR Result<TypeView,\ str> .
.TP
.B image_names()
The assembly names, e.g.\&
.BR \(dqAssembly\-CSharp.dll\(dq .
.TP
.B write_assemblies(dir)
Generate .NET proxy assemblies and write them to
.IR dir .
Returns
.BR Result<list<str>,\ str> .
.SH TypeView METHODS
.TP
.B name(), namespace(), full_name(), image_name()
The type's name parts and containing assembly.
.TP
.B flags()
The
.B TypeAttributes
flags as an integer.
.TP
.B base_type_name()
The parent type name, if any.
.TP
.B fields()
A list of
.BR FieldView .
.TP
.B methods()
A list of
.BR MethodView .
.SH FieldView METHODS
.TP
.B name(), type_name()
The field's name and type.
.TP
.B is_static()
Whether the field is static.
.SH MethodView METHODS
.TP
.B name(), return_type(), is_static()
The method's name, return type name, and whether it is static.
.TP
.B parameter_names(), parameter_type_names()
The parameter names and type names as lists of strings.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.RS
.nf
use std::re::dotnet::il2cpp;

fn main() -> Result<(), str> {
    let game = il2cpp::open("path/to/game")?;
    for ty in game.types() {
        io::println("{}", ty.full_name());
        for method in ty.methods() {
            io::println("  {}", method);
        }
    }
    game.write_assemblies("out")?;
    Ok(())
}
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xur (1),
